      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Campaigners hope move will force commercial banks to rethink holding assets linked to the fossil fuel</p><p>Climate campaigners have declared a victory after the Bank of England said it would no longer accept bonds linked to one of the most polluting industries on the planet for key loan arrangements.</p><p>The ban, which comes into force in October, marks a fresh crackdown on thermal coal, which is burned in power plants to create electricity, and has <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/25/bank-of-england-tackle-climate-crisis-mark-carney-greepeace\">long been a target of green policy activists</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jul/19/bank-of-england-bonds-coal-loans-assets\">Continue reading...</a>"
